Theorem RL-17: sharing-bound analysis (maximum simultaneous reference count)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-17 governs sharing-bound analysis per Annex E §AIMS RC Header
      Compression: "Sharing bound analysis SHALL determine the maximum
      simultaneous RC. is_local(s) AND Unique -> no header; straight-line N
      incs -> Bounded(N+1); loops / recursion / global -> Unbounded."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - DP-8 (is_local) <=> Locality IN {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal}; this
      replaces the former "NoEscape" term per RL-18a (Locality is the SSOT).
    - Shipped: target-system rule (ori_repr compress_arc_headers is a stubbed
      pass per repr.md sec-Shipped-vs-stubbed); realize/decide.rs supplies the
      sharing-bound inputs.
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-8 (is_local).

  Soundness property:
    Forall heap value v:

      (P1) Bound classification: RL-17 computes
        - NoHeader when is_local(v) AND Uniqueness(v) = Unique;
        - Bounded(N + 1) for straight-line code with N RcInc operations;
        - Unbounded when v is reachable through a loop, recursion, or global.

      (P2) Soundness: the computed bound is an UPPER bound on the simultaneous
           reference count — a local-unique value is never shared (NoHeader);
           straight-line code can create at most N + 1 references (the
           allocation plus N incs); loops / recursion / global reachability
           cannot be statically bounded (Unbounded is the conservative
           fallback).

    RL-17 is the analysis that RL-18 narrows the header width from; the bound
    must never UNDER-count (an under-count would narrow the header too far and
    overflow at runtime).

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via enumeration of the
    three bound classes.

    Part (P1/P2) — bound-classification grid:
      local_unique_no_header -> NoHeader
      straight_line_3_incs_bounded_4 -> Bounded(4)
      loop_recursion_global_unbounded -> Unbounded
      Coverage gate: 3 bound classes.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl17_sharing_bound; bound-
        classification enumeration; emits Fail on a misclassification)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-17 via the sharing-bound classification (local+Unique -> NoHeader; straight-line N incs -> Bounded(N+1); loop/recursion/global -> Unbounded) as an upper bound on simultaneous RC, grounded in the DP-8 is_local predicate and realize/decide.rs sharing-bound inputs
